Package: fastINFLECT
Title: Fast discovery of the metaclustering endpoint for SOM objects
Type: Package
Author: Jan VERHOEFF
Maintainer: Jan VERHOEFF <j.verhoeff@amsterdamumc.nl>
URL: https://mdmanurung.github.io/INFLECT, https://github.com/mdmanurung/INFLECT
BugReports: https://github.com/mdmanurung/INFLECT/issues
Description: Fast quality control and determination of optimal k for high-dimensional FlowSOM and kohonen SOM clustering data. fastINFLECT is a fast reimplementation of the original INFLECT package and keeps the core marker-unimodality method and the exported INFLECT() workflow while replacing the expensive repeated per-k quality-control loop with memoised hierarchy cuts, faster dip-test p-value lookup, and small compiled accelerators. It iteratively clusters and evaluates resulting clusters for marker unimodality, translates this into a unimodality score, and plots it into a diagnostic graph. On the fitted curve of this unimodality score fastINFLECT determines the inflection point where unimodality stops increasing for greater numbers of clusters.
